# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
#
# The lint job rebuilds the worker (`sh js/wasm-worker/build.sh`) before
# the wasm-stage gates run, so comparing the checked-in binary against the
# working tree costs nothing extra and fails exactly when a commit changed the
# worker sources or their seeds without shipping the rebuilt artifact. That is
# how the branch once fell back to the JS engine with no log line saying so.
# Plan 09 leaf 41 rewrote `engine_handler_precedence` and the precedence seed,
# the stale binary parsed the new seed into name-only rows, the browser worker
# permutation assert threw at init, and every E2E spec gated on the wasm worker
# status silently fell back (issue #1138).
#
# Issue #1569: two different causes fail this gate, and the bare diff could not
# tell them apart. A merged change to a worker input (rust/src/language.rs on
# 2026-11-14) and a new stable compiler (rustc 1.100.0 on 2026-11-13) both
# rebuild to different bytes. On failure `--explain` compares the inputs and
# the runner's compiler with data/meta/wasm-worker-inputs.lino and names the
# one that moved. Pull requests catch the first cause earlier: the fast
# JavaScript tier runs `node scripts/wasm-worker-inputs.mjs --check`.
ci_gate check-wasm-worker-current
  stage wasm
  description "The checked-in WASM worker binary matches a rebuild of its sources."
  run "git diff --exit-code -- js/formal_ai_worker.wasm || { node scripts/wasm-worker-inputs.mjs --explain; exit 1; }"
  justification "A stale WASM worker binary caused the browser to silently fall back to the JS engine with no log line when leaf 41 of plan 09 rewrote the precedence seed (#1138, commit 07b9990ea); this gate fails when the committed binary does not match a fresh rebuild."
